NOTES AND QUESTIONS ON FUENTES V. SHEVIN
1. Imagine that you are a state legislator trying to determine whether your state’s pre-judgment seizure laws are constitutional in the wake of Fuentes. What is the test you apply? Does Fuentes announce an absolute rule? A set of factors? An all-things-considered balancing? What characteristics of a state’s law would render it invalid? Which might guarantee its constitutionality?

2. To whom does the Due Process Clause apply? Which is unconstitutional under Fuentes: a replevin law that authorizes a creditor to have a sheriff repossess a stove after the creditor files an affidavit and posts a bond with the court, or a secured transactions statute that permits a creditor to have a private citizen repossess a stove with neither the filing of an affidavit nor the posting of a bond?

